Revision history for JS::Minifier

{{$NEXT}}

    - true/false shortening now parenthesizes when followed by **:
      `true ** 2` is shortened to `(!0)**2`, not the invalid `!0**2`
      (a unary expression cannot be the left operand of **)
    - The shebang line is always emitted first; a copyright banner is placed
      after it (on its own line), so `#!` scripts keep working
    - NOCOMPRESS and strip_debug are now handled inside the state machine
      instead of as regex pre-passes, so markers or ;;; lines that appear
      inside strings, template literals, or comments are no longer touched
      (previously they broke the input with "unterminated ..." errors)
    - The NUL-delimited NOCOMPRESS placeholder mechanism was removed; raw
      blocks are copied straight into the output
    - CLI: -o no longer truncates a file when the input file is also the
      output file (the output is opened lazily, after the input is read);
      --check now prints the actual error and rejects -o; unknown options
      are rejected; `--` ends option parsing; the version is parsed from
      META6.json without the (undeclared) JSON::Fast dependency
    - js-minifier: the :stream option now requires a Channel and dies with a
      clear message otherwise
    - README: line-terminator list corrected (form feed is whitespace but not
      a line terminator); --check and NOCOMPRESS normalization documented

    - State-machine rewrite of the minifier core (closure-lexical): the
      per-character state hash and ~20 state-passing functions are replaced
      by a closure with scalar window variables and inner subs. Output is
      byte-identical to the previous implementation on every option combo.
    - ~5.7x faster on a 441,600-char bundle (10.7s -> 1.9s plain mode);
      memory is lower too (no per-char hash lookups)
    - Added a differential regression test (t/06-differential) backed by
      5,403 captured goldens covering 491 inputs x 11 option combos, plus a
      benchmark script (xt/bench.raku)

    - Aggressive mode is now ASI-safe: newlines that separate statements
      are preserved (no longer silently producing invalid or semantically
      changed output for semicolon-less code); whitespace before '.' is
      stripped for compact member chains
    - CLI: -o/--output and -c/--copyright now error when their value is
      missing; -o no longer truncates a file when run interactively with
      no input

    - Initial release: a fork of JS::Minify by Sam Morrison, rewritten for
      performance and reliability
    - New CLI tool bin/jsminify
    - Shebang, bang-comment, template literal, and NOCOMPRESS support
    - drop_console/drop_debugger options; true/false shortened in value
      contexts; semicolons removed before closing braces
    - Numerous bug fixes (out-of-bounds reads, line continuation,
      unterminated string detection, division/regex misclassification,
      CRLF normalization, U+2028/U+2029 line terminators)
